# Performance

## Framework semantics

Most CakePHP performance issues are ORM-shaped: N+1 contains, over-eager association graphs, unbounded lists, and missing pagination. Caching exists (`Cache` engine) but is not a substitute for correct query ownership.

## Required behavior

- Prefer pagination for large lists; avoid unbounded `all()` in HTTP paths.
- Use `contain` deliberately; prefer matching/select narrowing when filtering.
- Detect and fix hidden N+1 (loops that re-query associations).
- Cache derived/expensive reads only with explicit invalidation strategy when the project already uses Cache.
- Do not add Redis/custom caches by default for a single finder.

## Anti-patterns

- hidden-n-plus-one
- over-eager-contain
- Caching as a band-aid for fat controllers / bad queries

## Review checklist

- [ ] List endpoints paginated or explicitly bounded
- [ ] Association graphs justified per use case
- [ ] No unexplained per-row queries in loops
